CITY BATTLES · AUG – OCT 2026EVENTPowered byLEGAL · TERMS AND CONDITIONSLAST UPDATED · 10 SEP 2026Terms & conditions.The rules of the road for participating in the iQOO Hackathon 2026 City Battles. Covers every city battle and the Grand Finale.01Definitions and acceptanceIn these Terms, "Organisers" means Reskilll and iQOO (a brand of vivo Mobile India Private Limited), together with their respective affiliates, sponsors, partners, agents and personnel; "Event" means the iQOO Hackathon 2026, comprising each City Battle, every online or on-site round and the Grand Finale; and "Participant" means any person who registers for, applies to, or takes part in the Event.By registering for the Event or otherwise using this platform, you confirm that you have read, understood and irrevocably accept these Terms, the Privacy Policy and the Code of Conduct, and that you have the legal capacity to do so. If you do not agree to any part of these Terms, you must not register for the Event or use this platform.02EligibilityThe Event is open to students and working professionals. Participants below eighteen (18) years of age may be required to furnish written parental or guardian consent as a condition of on-site attendance. Teams comprise one (1) to three (3) builders; solo Participants may be matched into a team at the Organisers' discretion. The Organisers may require documentary proof of identity, age, student status or employment at any stage, and may reject or disqualify any registration for which such proof is not furnished to their satisfaction.03Code of conductParticipants shall conduct themselves with respect and professionalism. Harassment, discrimination, intimidation and unsafe behaviour are prohibited. Submissions must be the original work of the team, created during the Event (pre-Event drafting of ideas is permitted). Third-party APIs and open-source libraries may be used subject to their licences and to proper attribution. Plagiarism, misrepresentation of authorship and the submission of work developed for or submitted to another competition are grounds for immediate disqualification.04Submissions and intellectual propertyYou retain all intellectual property rights in your submission. By submitting, you grant the Organisers a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide, irrevocable licence to receive, store, review, evaluate, reproduce, publish and showcase your submission, your team name and your city, for purposes connected with the Event and its promotion, in perpetuity. Any commercial exploitation beyond such showcase shall require a separate written agreement. You warrant that your submission does not infringe the rights of any third party and that you are entitled to grant this licence, and you shall indemnify the Organisers against any claim to the contrary.05iQOO loaner hardwareDevices issued at check-in remain at all times the property of iQOO and are loaned on a bailment basis for the duration of the Event only. You shall use such hardware with due care, shall not modify, unlock, encumber or part with possession of it, and shall return it in working condition at the close of the Event. Loss, theft or damage may be recovered from the team, jointly and severally, at replacement value.06Selection, evaluation and shortlistingApplications, ideas and submissions are assessed on a comparative basis against evaluation rubrics framed by the Organisers, which may include, without limitation, originality, technical merit, feasibility, quality of execution, relevance to the declared track or problem statement, demonstrated or potential impact, and the completeness and clarity of the submission. The rubrics, their weightages, any qualifying cut-off, and the constitution of the evaluation panel are determined by the Organisers and may be framed, revised or applied differently at any stage or for any round, city or track.Admission to a City Battle, shortlisting for any on-site round, and selection for the Grand Finale are made at the sole, absolute and unfettered discretion of the Organisers, on the merits and demerits of each application as assessed by them. Scores, rankings, evaluator notes and the reasons for non-selection are confidential, shall not be disclosed, and shall not be the subject of any request for inspection. No correspondence, representation, appeal, re-evaluation or re-scoring shall be entertained. All decisions of the Organisers and of the jury are final and binding upon all Participants, and participation in the Event constitutes acceptance of this clause.07Judging, prizes and taxesThe decision of the jury is final. Prize money, where awarded, shall be disbursed to the registered team leader on behalf of the team, against such documentation as the Organisers may require, and the team shall be solely responsible for its internal apportionment. All prizes are subject to deduction of tax at source and to applicable statutory levies; all further tax obligations rest with the recipients. Prizes are non-transferable and non-negotiable, may not be exchanged for cash or any alternative, and the Organisers reserve the right to substitute any prize with one of comparable value. The Organisers are under no obligation to award all or any of the prizes announced where, in their assessment, no entry meets the requisite standard.08Right of admission and right of refusalThe Organisers reserve the right of admission to the Event and to every venue at which it is held. The Organisers may, at their sole discretion, without assigning any reason and without liability of any nature, decline, suspend, withdraw or cancel any registration; refuse entry to, or require the departure of, any person from a venue; reject or withhold any submission; disqualify any Participant or team; and withhold, revoke or recall any prize, benefit, certificate or recognition, whether before, during or after the Event.Such action may be taken on grounds including, without limitation, ineligibility; incomplete, false, misleading or duplicated information; plagiarism or misappropriation of third-party work; breach of the Code of Conduct or of these Terms; non-compliance with venue, safety or security requirements or with any lawful direction of the Organisers; or any conduct prejudicial to the interests, safety or reputation of the Organisers, their partners or other Participants. The publication of tracks, prize pools, schedules or shortlisting criteria constitutes an invitation to participate and not an offer, and creates no right or entitlement in favour of any person. The Organisers may modify, substitute, reschedule, curtail, suspend or cancel any round, city battle, track or prize at any time.09Force majeureThe Organisers shall not be liable for any failure, delay, curtailment or cancellation arising from any cause beyond their reasonable control, including acts of God, fire, flood, earthquake, epidemic or pandemic, war, terrorism, civil unrest, strike or labour disturbance, any order, restriction or direction of any government or statutory authority, venue unavailability, or the failure or interruption of power, internet, telecommunication or third-party platform services.10Limitation of liabilityParticipation in the Event is voluntary and at the Participant's own risk. To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Organisers shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, punitive or consequential loss, or for any loss of profit, opportunity, data or goodwill, arising out of or in connection with participation in the Event, the use of loaner hardware, travel to or attendance at any venue, or the availability of this platform. The aggregate liability of the Organisers, in contract, tort or otherwise, shall in no event exceed the aggregate fees paid by the Participant to the Organisers in connection with the Event, which for this Event is nil. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability which cannot lawfully be excluded.City Battles are physical, in-person events which run for thirty (30) hours overnight. Each Participant is responsible for their own health, including any pre-existing medical condition, and shall inform the Organisers in advance of anything requiring arrangement — medication, allergies, and accessibility or dietary requirements. Given such notice the Organisers will endeavour to accommodate the requirement. The Organisers shall not be liable for any medical condition, illness or injury arising during or out of participation, save where such liability cannot be excluded by law.11Amendment of these termsThe Organisers may amend these Terms at any time. Material amendments will be notified by email to the address furnished at registration and published on this page, with the "last updated" date revised accordingly. Continued participation in the Event or continued use of this platform after such publication constitutes acceptance of the amended Terms.12Governing law, dispute resolution and jurisdictionThese Terms, and any dispute, difference or claim arising out of or in connection with them or with participation in the Event, including any question as to their existence, validity, interpretation, breach or termination, and whether contractual or non-contractual, shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India, without regard to any conflict of laws principle.The parties shall first endeavour to resolve any such dispute amicably by discussion, commenced by written notice from the aggrieved party. If the dispute is not resolved within thirty (30) days of such notice, it shall be referred to and finally resolved by arbitration under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, and any statutory modification thereof, before a sole arbitrator appointed by mutual agreement of the parties and, failing such agreement, appointed in accordance with the said Act. The seat and venue of arbitration shall be New Delhi, the proceedings shall be conducted in English, and the award shall be final and binding upon the parties.Subject to the foregoing, the courts at New Delhi shall have exclusive jurisdiction over all matters arising out of or in connection with these Terms and the Event, and each Participant irrevocably submits to that jurisdiction and waives any objection on the ground of venue or forum non conveniens.13GeneralIf any provision of these Terms is held to be invalid or unenforceable, that provision shall be severed and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect. No failure or delay by the Organisers in exercising any right shall operate as a waiver of it, and no single or partial exercise shall preclude any further exercise. These Terms, read with the Privacy Policy and the Code of Conduct, constitute the entire agreement between the Participant and the Organisers in respect of the Event, and supersede all prior representations and understandings. Nothing in these Terms creates any partnership, joint venture, agency or employment relationship. Participants may not assign their rights or obligations; the Organisers may assign or novate theirs to an affiliate or successor. Clause headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation.QuestionsReach the organizing team at sameera@reskilll.com.iQOO HACKATHON 2026 · CITY BATTLES · 4 CITIES · AUG – OCT 2026GuidePrivacyTermsPOWERED BY RESKILLL
--- END UNTRUSTED EXTERNAL CONTENT ---
