 buckets, but teams cannot mix: all students or all working professionals. Solo or teams of 1–3.One city battleRegister for one of the four city venues (TBA). You attend that city battle in person after shortlisting, not online.On-device AILocal and open-source models on the Snapdragon NPU, with Office Kit bridging the phone to deeper laptop compute when you need it. AI credits for the weekend are free.30-hour buildClock starts Saturday 10:00. Active hacking from 11:00. Green Light (both devices) and Red Light (phone-only via Office Kit) keep the build phone-first through Sunday awards.What you can build.The full slate. Each track's label says where it runs — city battles, the Grand Finale, or both. A local or open-source model at the core earns brownie points, with the phone in the loop via Office Kit.TRACK 01FinTech and CommerceCity battles onlyMoney, payments, commerce, lending, investing, and financial inclusion — built for how India actually transacts.TRACK 02Smart EducationCity battles onlyBuild AI-powered learning: tutoring, study workflows, assessment, skilling, and the daily operations of a classroom.TRACK 03HealthTechCity battles onlyBuild AI-powered healthcare, wellness, fitness, or mental health solutions.TRACK 04ProductivityCity battles + FinaleBuild AI-powered solutions that help people work smarter, automate repetitive tasks, manage time and information, improve workflows, and get more done.TRACK 05Smart LivingCity battles + FinaleDesign AI-powered solutions for smart homes, IoT, connected devices, or everyday convenience.TRACK 06Developer ToolsCity battles + FinaleBuild tools that help developers create, test, deploy, or collaborate faster using AI.TRACK 07MobilityGrand Finale onlyBuild solutions for navigation, EVs, public transport, parking, or travel experiences.TRACK 08Community AppGrand Finale onlyBuild a community app, not specific to iQOO, that connects developers, professionals, or interest groups, with AI (preferred to be on device) at the core.TRACK 09Open InnovationWildcard · everywhereAnything outside the tracks, any domain, with a local or open source model at the core.Register for a city battle and pick your track from the dashboard.How we score.Six dimensions. 100% total.End product quality: Jury panel. Does it work, is it useful, would someone keep using it.30%Novelty and impact: Jury panel. Originality and real-world impact.20%HackTracker · creative phone use: Device data. Camera, voice, on-device AI in the build.15%Technical depth: Jury panel. Architecture, code quality, robustness, real use of the hardware.15%HackTracker · Office Kit usage: Device data. Phone and laptop bridge use.10%Demo and presentation: Jury panel. A compelling 3 to 5 minute pitch.10%Total100%Top 6 teams per city advance to the Grand Finale (Oct 9–11, 2026), three from each bucket. Prize pool: ₹40,00,000 across city battles, finale, and special track awards.Rules & guidelines.Please read before you build.Phone-first formatThe iQOO device is the build surface and the demo surface: every entry must run and pitch on the phone.A local or open-source model at the core earns brownie points, with the phone in the loop via Office Kit.Office Kit bridges phone and laptop (screen mirror, clipboard, file transfer, remote control). Pairing instructions ship with the loaner and are covered in the Saturday 10:00 teach-in. On-device inference targets the Snapdragon NPU. AI credits for the weekend are free.Stacks welcome: native Android, Flutter, React Native, or PWA. If it runs on the phone with a local or open-source model at the core, it qualifies.30-hour city battleEach City Battle is a 30-hour all-inclusive event: Sat around 08:00 check-in through Sun around 17:00 awards.Green Light = both devices; Red Light = iQOO phone only via Office Kit. Two evaluation rounds (Sat evening, Sun morning) feed a Top 10 pitch.Top 6 teams per city advance to the Grand Finale in Bengaluru on Oct 9–11, 2026: 3 student teams and 3 working-professional teams. The Finale itself runs 48 hours, Friday evening to Sunday evening. Standout teams beyond the Top 6 can also earn Finale slots, and you can register directly for the Grand Finale without going through a city battle.Your iQOO deviceOne flagship iQOO loaner phone per person, handed over at Saturday check-in with HackTracker pre-installed and Office Kit already paired.Devices remain iQOO property. Keep them in the venue / designated hacking zone and return them before exit.HackTracker captures counts and durations only (no keystrokes, screenshots, or browsing) for creative phone use and Office Kit scoring.Tracks & bucketsSeven tracks in the city battles; the Grand Finale runs six, dropping FinTech and Commerce, Smart Education and HealthTech and adding Mobility and Community App.Tracks are open to students and working professionals, but teams cannot mix buckets.Tracks are broad domains, not fixed briefs. Anything that fits is fair game. Open Innovation is the wildcard everywhere.Build rulesOriginal work only: code written during the event window. No shipping a pre-built product.Open-source libraries and frameworks are fine with attribution; carrying in a completed app is not.Submit your repo and demo assets on the Reskilll platform before the hard cutoff (repos locked before Top 10 pitches). Late submissions may incur scoring penalties or disqualification.Cheating, plagiarism, or unfair practice means immediate disqualification. Organisers may verify a project was built inside the event window.JudgingTwo scored evaluation rounds plus a Top 10 final pitch, demo on the iQOO phone. HackTracker supplies phone-use and Office Kit scores; jury scores product quality, novelty, depth, and pitch.Weights: End product 30% · Novelty 20% · Creative phone use 15% · Technical depth 15% · Office Kit 10% · Demo 10%.Top 6 teams per city advance (three per bucket); standouts beyond Top 6 can also earn Finale slots. Hit a technical issue before your slot? Tell an organiser immediately.Code of conductRespect everyone: participants, mentors, jury, organisers, volunteers. Every background and skill level is welcome.Zero tolerance for harassment, discrimination, intimidation, or disruptive behaviour: immediate removal.Help others debug when you can. If something feels wrong, speak to any organiser immediately.Venue rulesReport on time: check-in closes per the city schedule.No smoking on premises. No alcohol on-site.Stay in designated zones (hacking floor, rest area, meal zone). Keep noise considerate of neighbouring teams.Safety & wellbeingFirst-aid support is on site. In an emergency, alert the nearest organiser immediately.Take breaks: a team that rests ships better code, especially through the night sprint.Tell a teammate or volunteer if you step out after dark.Tell us in advance about anything we need to plan around — a medical condition, an allergy, medication that needs storing, an accessibility requirement or a dietary restriction. Reply to your confirmation email or call your city contact. With notice we can arrange a great deal; on the morning itself, very little.You take part at your own risk and stay responsible for your own health, including any condition you already have. Reskilll and iQOO are not liable for medical issues arising during the event — the Terms below set out the full position.Reaching organisersOn the floor: grab any organiser or volunteer at any time.A direct contact is shared at check-in. The query desk stays open through close.Series contact: sameera@reskilll.comPhotography & mediaEvent filming and photography support iQOO and Reskilll documentation and promotion.Consent at check-in covers event media use. Do not film or share another team’s screen or build without permission.Standard TermsEligibility, intellectual property, loaner-hardware responsibility, prizes and tax, liability, and how these rules can change are all covered in one place.Read the Terms & ConditionsIn SummaryBuild phone-first. Compete for your city. Advance to the finale. Be good to each other. We’ve got you for every hour of the weekend.IP & data.IP RIGHTSYou retain IP on your submission. Participating grants iQOO and Reskilll a non-exclusive, royalty-free right to review, evaluate, and showcase the work for hackathon-related communications.DATA PRIVACYSubmissions and supporting docs are treated as confidential, accessed only by the organizing team. Any use beyond showcase requires a separate written agreement.iQOO HACKATHON 2026 · CITY BATTLES · 4 CITIES · AUG – OCT 2026GuidePrivacyTermsPOWERED BY RESKILLL
