../shared/faq.txt-1-01
../shared/faq.txt-2-Who can participate?
../shared/faq.txt-3-
../shared/faq.txt:4:Students and working professionals (IT and white collar) across India. Every track is open to both buckets, but teams cannot mix: a team is either all students or all working professionals. Register solo or as a team of 1–3. You attend one city battle in person after shortlisting.
../shared/faq.txt-5-=====
../shared/faq.txt-6-02
../shared/faq.txt-7-What is the format?
../shared/faq.txt-8-
../shared/faq.txt-9-A 30-hour phone-first battle: Saturday 10:00 to Sunday around 17:00. Active hacking from 11:00 with Green Light (both devices) and Red Light (iQOO phone only via Office Kit). Two evaluation rounds feed a Top 10 pitch, then awards.
../shared/faq.txt-10-=====
--
../shared/faq.txt-20-=====
../shared/faq.txt-21-05
../shared/faq.txt-22-What can I build?
../shared/faq.txt-23-
../shared/faq.txt:24:City battles run seven tracks: FinTech and Commerce, Smart Education, HealthTech, Productivity, Smart Living, Developer Tools and Open Innovation. The Grand Finale runs six: Mobility, Community App, Smart Living, Productivity, Developer Tools and Open Innovation. Tracks are broad domains, not fixed briefs. A local or open-source model at the core earns brownie points; keep the phone in the loop via Office Kit. Open Innovation is the wildcard everywhere.
../shared/faq.txt-25-=====
../shared/faq.txt-26-06
../shared/faq.txt-27-What is the prize pool?
../shared/faq.txt-28-
../shared/faq.txt-29-The total pool is ₹40,00,000 across the four city battles and the Grand Finale. Each city targets ₹6L split across working professionals (₹3.2L) and students (₹2.8L). Final numbers are set by iQOO.
../shared/faq.txt-30-=====
../shared/faq.txt-31-07
../shared/faq.txt-32-What stack can I use?
../shared/faq.txt-33-
../shared/faq.txt:34:Anything that runs on the phone: native Android, Flutter, React Native, or PWA. You demo on the iQOO device, and a local or open-source model at the core earns brownie points. On-device inference targets the Snapdragon NPU (Sarvam, Gemma, Phi class models). Office Kit bridges to the laptop when you need deeper compute.
../shared/faq.txt-35-=====
../shared/faq.txt-36-08
../shared/faq.txt-37-How does shortlisting work?
../shared/faq.txt-38-
../shared/faq.txt-39-Registration is open to anyone, and every entry goes through idea screening to shortlist builders for the on-ground battle. Scoring weights novelty, tech impact, problem choice, idea/scope fit for 30 hours, and phone-first fit. Registration is free.
../shared/faq.txt-40-=====

